// The storyteller (storyteller demo 1.svg, added to the workbench
// 2026-07-26 at Kimia's request) — the Storytellers-category archetype,
// an imported hand-drawn illustration like the signer. It is built from
// SIX stacked shade layers, lightest painted first and darker shades
// stacked on top, so the layers model the figure's light and depth. As
// with the signer we keep that layer structure and only swap the shade
// RAMP, letting one drawing be shown in any candidate body colour.
//
// Unlike the signer (a bare colour test), the storyteller ships ASSEMBLED
// per the friend recipe (design-bible §3, §7, §9c):
//   • the two small near-white eye placeholders Kimia traced into the
//     drawing are NOT rendered — the canonical yellow <Eye/> (eye.jsx:
//     fixed yellow orb in its own dark socket, always a different colour
//     from the body) is mounted at their exact centres and sizes instead;
//   • the body glows its OWN body colour (never the eyes' yellow): the
//     bottom layer, blurred and filled with the palette's glow colour,
//     sits behind the figure — the same aura recipe as the Drifter;
//   • each eye sits in its own .storyteller-eye-blink wrapper so the
//     idle blink (index.css) squashes it around its own centre — and the
//     eyes live in a SEPARATE overlay svg from the heavy body (see the
//     note above StorytellerBodyDefs for why that split is load-bearing).
//
// COLOURS ARE STAND-INS. TODO(T5.2): move the ramps into the CSS
// design-tokens file once it exists, like every other asset here.

import { Eye, EyeDefs } from './eye.jsx'
export { EyeDefs }

